# MCP Server Implementation Guidelines

## Public tool interface (POC)
- `connect_wordpress`
- `build_wp_index`
- `get_index_status`
- `audit_component`
- `find_similar_content`
- `where_is_used`
- `query_wp_db_readonly` (single `SELECT` via `wp db query`, allowlisted read-only)
- `get_theme_profile`
- `get_design_bridge_readiness`
- `bridge_design_to_implementation`

## Internal helpers (transport hidden from user prompts)
- `run_wp_cli`
- `search_wp_files`
- `read_wp_file`
- `apply_patch`

## Validation & security
- Reject any request that attempts to access paths outside WP root.
- `run_wp_cli`: implement an allowlist of commands/subcommands.
- `query_wp_db_readonly`: reject anything except a single validated read-only `SELECT` (no DDL/DML, no cross-schema reads); cap row output via `LIMIT`.
- `apply_patch`: require unified diff format and validate file targets exist within WP root.

## Logging
- Log inputs/outputs with redaction for secrets.
- Return structured errors with stable codes (e.g., WPCLI_NOT_FOUND, WP_ROOT_INVALID).
